# gtk3 -- GTK 3, built Wayland-only, and packaged for exactly one reason.
#
# THIS LOOKS WRONG IN A TREE WHOSE README SAYS "a complete GTK 4 application
# platform", so the reason is written here rather than left to be re-derived:
#
#   gnome-control-center 48.4's meson.build, lines 298-306, requires
#   libnma-gtk4 unconditionally under host_is_linux -- no required:false, and
#   meson_options.txt has NO network option at all, so no -D switch can drop
#   it. Without it, Settings does not configure networking.
#
#   libnma 1.10.6's meson.build line 159 has a TOP-LEVEL, UNCONDITIONAL
#   gtk+-3.0 dependency. -Dlibnma_gtk4=true does not replace that, it ADDS a
#   GTK 4 library beside it. So the GTK 4 network widgets that
#   gnome-control-center needs cannot be built without GTK 3 present.
#
# The README says "Wayland first", not "GTK 4 only" -- and it already packages
# the X client libraries while running no X server, for the same kind of reason.
# This is that policy applied once more, not an exception to it.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env -- versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh.
#
# NOT ON download.gnome.org UNDER THE NAME YOU EXPECT: the module is `gtk`, not
# `gtk+`, even for the 3.24 series -- /sources/gtk+/3.24/ does not exist. The
# sha256 below was checked against upstream's own published
# gtk-3.24.50.sha256sum rather than only against the downloaded bytes, which is
# the difference between "what I fetched" and "what upstream released".
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/gtk/3.24/gtk-3.24.50.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=399118a5699314622165a11b769ea9b6ed68e037b6d46d57cfcf4851dec07529
SRC_DIR=gtk-3.24.50

# -Dx11_backend=false -Dwayland_backend=true. THE POINT OF THE PACKAGE'S SHAPE.
# Both default to TRUE, so leaving either alone builds an X11 GTK 3 and links
# libX11, libXi, libXrandr and the rest into libgdk-3 -- on a system with no X
# server. post-install.sh asserts the OUTCOME rather than trusting the flag:
# gtk+-3.0.pc carries a `targets=` variable built from the enabled backends
# (meson.build 954-965), and gdkconfig.h defines GDK_WINDOWING_X11 only when
# x11 is on. Both are checked.
#
# -Dbroadway_backend=false is already the default and is named so it stays a
# decision; it is an HTTP/websocket display backend and nothing here wants one.
#
# -Dxinerama=no. DEFAULTS TO 'auto', AND THIS TREE SHIPS THE X CLIENT
# LIBRARIES -- which is finding 4 exactly: an auto feature in a tree that has
# the dependency switches itself on. It is meaningless without the X11 backend,
# so it would be an X dependency acquired for a backend that is not built.
#
# -Dcolord=no. Also 'auto', and colord belongs to another chain. Today it
# resolves off because colord is absent; the moment that package lands, an
# unpinned `auto` would silently add a dependency to a rebuild of THIS package,
# and nothing in the recipe would have changed to explain it. Pinned so the
# answer does not depend on what else has been merged.
#
# -Dprint_backends=file,lpr. The default 'auto' is worse than it looks:
# modules/printbackends/meson.build line 20 sets print_strict_deps=false for
# auto, so a backend whose dependencies are missing is SILENTLY DROPPED, while
# an explicit list makes a missing dependency a hard error. cups is another
# chain's package; with 'auto', gtk3 would quietly gain a cups print backend
# the first time it was rebuilt after cups landed. `file` is mandatory on unix
# (line 37 errors without it) and `lpr` only spawns the lpr command, so neither
# adds a dependency.
#
# -Ddemos=false -Dexamples=false -Dtests=false. All three default TRUE. They
# build gtk3-demo, gtk3-widget-factory and a large test suite that nothing here
# runs; demos and examples also install binaries into /usr/bin.
#
# -Dgtk_doc=false -Dman=false are the defaults, named because both would need
# tooling that is not packaged.
#
# -Dintrospection=true is the default and is required: libnma builds GObject
# introspection data against GTK 3, and gnome-control-center reaches it through
# that. Declaring it means declaring gobject-introspection AND glib-introspection
# -- the scanner and the typelibs it reads are different packages.
MESON_ARGS="-Dx11_backend=false -Dwayland_backend=true -Dbroadway_backend=false \
-Dxinerama=no -Dcolord=no -Dprint_backends=file,lpr \
-Dcloudproviders=false -Dtracker3=false -Dprofiler=false \
-Ddemos=false -Dexamples=false -Dtests=false -Dinstalled_tests=false \
-Dgtk_doc=false -Dman=false -Dintrospection=true"
